                    <msContents>
                        <summary>Commentary on Al-Ṭūsī's Taḥrīr al-Majisṭī by Niẓām al-Dīn al-Ḥasan
                            ibn Muḥammad Nīsābūrī.</summary>
                        <msItem xml:id="manuscript_13998_item_1">
                            <locus from="1b" to="397a">1b-397a</locus>
                            <title xml:lang="ar-Latn-x-lc" key="">Tafsīr al-Taḥrīr</title>
                            <title xml:lang="ar" type="alt">تفسير التحرير</title>
                            <title xml:lang="en" type="alt">Explanation of the Writing</title>
                            <author key="person_36360883">
                                <persName xml:lang="en">Nīsābūrī, Niẓām al-Dīn al-Ḥasan ibn
                                    Muḥammad, -1328 or 1329</persName>
                                <persName xml:lang="ar">النيسابوري، نظام الدين الحسن بن محمد،
                                    توفي</persName>
                            </author>
                            <note><p>The title of the work is given by <ref
                                        target="https://archive.org/details/kashfalzunun05hajiuoft/page/385/mode/2up"
                                        >Ḥaj. Khal. (v, 386)</ref> as <quote xml:lang="ar">تغيير
                                        التحرير</quote>.</p>
                                <p>The author mentions in his introduction <name
                                        key="person_236145542748996641711"><persName>Maḥmūd bin
                                            Masʿūd al-Shīrāzī</persName> (<persName>محمود بن مسعود
                                        </persName>الشيرازي)</name>.</p>
                                <p>The work ends abruptly, but as the final leaf represents the
                                    second leaf of the ninth faṣl of the 13th maqālah, only two
                                    short faṣls are lost, equivalent perhaps to four or 5 leaves at
                                    the utmost.</p>
                                <p>The book is divided into 13 maqālahs and many faṣls.</p>
                                <p>The words commented upon are introduced by <quote>قوله</quote>,
                                    and those of the commentary by <quote>اقول</quote>, both
                                    rubricated. </p></note>
                            <textLang mainLang="ar">Arabic</textLang>
                            <incipit>السعد قرين من صدر كلامه بالحمد لواهب العادة واليمين</incipit>

                            <listBibl>
                                <bibl><ref
                                        target="https://archive.org/details/kashfalzunun05hajiuoft/page/385/mode/2up"
                                        >Haji Khalfah, <title>Kashf al-zunun - Lexicon
                                            Bibliographicum et Encyclopaedicum</title>, vol. 5
                                        (London: Oriental Translation Fund, 1835), 386.</ref></bibl>
                            </listBibl>
                        </msItem>
                    </msContents>
